\ Stack residue left by the loop combinators when the predicate or the body raises.
\
\ `loop` and `(until-loop)` carry their predicate across the flag test. `while` recurses
\ through `loop` and `until` through `(until-loop)`.
\
\ `recover` does not restore stack depth, and the harness prints the stack after every
\ line, so each probe's leftover is pinned in the golden.
\
\ The tail-call probes at the end complete only if the recursion step propagates through
\ `if`; otherwise the nested frames overflow the native stack.

\ loop: the predicate raises on the first iteration
[ 10 [ 1 0 / ] loop ] [ error-type: @get >string print-line ] recover
wipe

\ loop: the predicate raises on the third iteration, after two counted rounds
[ 0 [ 1 + dup 3 = [ 1 0 / ] when dup 5 < ] loop ] [ error-type: @get >string print-line ] recover
wipe

\ loop: a user throw in the predicate
[ 0 [ 1 + dup 2 = [ f "boom" test-error: make-error throw ] when dup 5 < ] loop ] [ error-type: @get >string print-line ] recover
wipe

\ while: the predicate raises
[ 0 [ dup 2 = [ 1 0 / ] when dup 5 < ] [ 1 + ] while ] [ error-type: @get >string print-line ] recover
wipe

\ while: the body raises
[ 0 [ dup 5 < ] [ 1 + dup 2 = [ 1 0 / ] when ] while ] [ error-type: @get >string print-line ] recover
wipe

\ until: the predicate raises
[ 0 [ dup 2 = [ 1 0 / ] when dup 5 >= ] [ 1 + ] until ] [ error-type: @get >string print-line ] recover
wipe

\ until: the body raises
[ 0 [ dup 5 >= ] [ 1 + dup 2 = [ 1 0 / ] when ] until ] [ error-type: @get >string print-line ] recover
wipe

\ nested: an inner loop's predicate raises inside an outer loop's predicate
[ 0 [ 1 + 0 [ 1 + dup 2 = [ 1 0 / ] when dup 3 < ] loop drop dup 5 < ] loop ] [ error-type: @get >string print-line ] recover
wipe

\ truthiness: a non-boolean predicate result continues the loop
0 [ 1 + dup 3 < [ 0 ] [ f ] if ] loop >string print-line

\ truthiness: a non-boolean predicate result stops `until`
0 [ 1 + dup 3 < [ f ] [ 0 ] if ] [ ] until >string print-line

\ tail calls: 100000 iterations through each combinator
0 [ 1 + dup 100000 < ] loop >string print-line
100000 [ dup 0 > ] [ 1 - ] while >string print-line
100000 [ dup 1 < ] [ 1 - ] until >string print-line
